You need a function that accepts any number of arguments and returns their sum. It must also be curriable: `sum(1)(2)(3)()` should return 6. Which implementation is correct?

```js
// A
function sum(...args) { return args.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0); }

// B
function sum(a) { return function(b) { return a + b; }; }

// C
function sum(...args) {
  return function(...more) {
    if (more.length === 0) return args.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
    return sum(...args, ...more);
  };
}

// D
const sum = new Proxy(Function, { apply: (t, _, args) => args.reduce((a,b) => a+b,0) });
```

A developer notices that an async function inside a forEach loop doesn't seem to await properly:

```js
const results = [];
[1,2,3].forEach(async (n) => {
  const res = await fetchData(n);
  results.push(res);
});
console.log(results); // always []
```

What is the correct fix?

You need to debounce a search input so the API is called 300ms after the user stops typing. Which implementation is correct?

```js
// A
function debounce(fn, delay) {
  let timer;
  return function(...args) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), delay);
  };
}

// B
function debounce(fn, delay) {
  return function(...args) {
    setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), delay);
  };
}

// C
function debounce(fn, delay) {
  let timer;
  return function(...args) {
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), delay);
  };
}
```

What does the following code output and why?

```js
async function main() {
  try {
    setTimeout(() => { throw new Error('oops'); }, 0);
  } catch(e) {
    console.log('caught:', e.message);
  }
}
main();
```

What does this output?

```js
const obj = {
  value: 42,
  getValue: function() { return this.value; },
  getValueArrow: () => this.value
};
console.log(obj.getValue());
console.log(obj.getValueArrow());
```
